FINAL ANSWER:
Short answer: no part of the codebase depends on a single contributor. Two people hold most of the knowledge, and both are now inactive.

**Overall**
- The repo has 326 non-merge commits from 64 authors, spanning 2013-01-30 to 2026-04-12.
- The bus factor is 2. Douglas Christopher Wilson (143 commits, 43.9%) and Troy Goode (95 commits, 29.1%) together cover more than 50% of commits. dependabot is next at 11 commits, and no one else has more than 4.
- The tool's silo rule flags a directory when one author made more than 80% of its commits. No directory is flagged:

| Directory | Commits | Authors | Top author | Top author's share |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| root | 233 | 42 | Wilson | 51% |
| `lib` | 66 | 25 | Goode | 50% |
| `test` | 72 | 18 | Goode | 44% |
| `.github` | 27 | 7 | Wilson | 37% |

**Single-owner files**

These are the files where line ownership is concentrated in one person. Ownership here is the share of lines at HEAD, from `git blame`.
- Wilson owns `.eslintrc.yml`, `test/.eslintrc.yml` and `test/support/env.js`, which are tiny config files. He is also the main owner of `HISTORY.md` (78%), `LICENSE` (77%), `.gitignore` (80%), `package.json` (48%) and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (49%). His last commit was 2021-09-07.
- Goode owns `test/vary.js` (100%), `test/issue-2.js` (83%) and `README.md` (38%). His last commit was 2026-04-10.
- Some CI files have a single owner who is no longer active:
  - `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml`: Íñigo Marquínez Prado (93%), last commit 2024-05-14.
  - `.github/workflows/codeql.yml`: Sebastian Beltran (95%), last commit 2025-07-23.
  - `.github/dependabot.yml`: Ulises Gascón (100%), last commit 2026-01-22.

**Two caveats on the tool's output**
- The "Fiona Formatter" figure is misleading. The tool reports her as owning 50.9% of lines, including `lib/index.js` (90%) and `test/test.js` (94%). All of that comes from the style commit `62628c0` (4-space indent and double quotes), which rewrote whitespace. Ignoring that commit with `git blame --ignore-rev`, the real `lib/index.js` owners are Goode (109 lines), Fiona Formatter (57), Wilson (36) and Raymond Feng (8). For `test/test.js` they are Wilson (270), Goode (213) and Fiona Formatter (178). `test/example-app.js` and `test/error-response.js` are mostly Goode's work (66 of 81 and 56 of 66 lines). I did not re-run the rest of the files this way.
- The tool reports all 18 files as orphaned, but I don't trust that count. It treats "inactive" as no commit since 2026-04-22, six months before today (2026-10-22), and the repo's last commit was 2026-04-12. So every author counts as inactive, including Goode. That says the repo has had no commits for six months. It does not show that any particular person has left.

**Recommendation**
- The core logic in `lib/index.js` is shared mainly by Goode and Wilson. If either leaves, the other is the only person with deep history there.
- The highest-risk files are the CI and security workflows (`scorecard.yml`, `codeql.yml`, `dependabot.yml`). Each was written by one person who is no longer committing.
- If you want, I can run `knowledge_risk` or `blame_summary` on `lib/` alone with the style commit excluded.
